{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "intro_cell"
   },
   "source": [
    "# 🚀 MultiTalk Colab Notebook 🚀\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Welcome! This notebook will guide you through generating a video with MultiTalk. This project is officially from [MeiGen-AI/MultiTalk](https://github.com/MeiGen-AI/MultiTalk).\\n",
    "\\n",
    "### **Step 1: Setup Environment**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Run the following cell to clone the repository and install all the necessary dependencies. This will take a few minutes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "install_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('🚀 Cloning repository...')\\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/MeiGen-AI/MultiTalk.git\\n",
    "%cd MultiTalk\\n",
    "print('✅ Repository cloned.')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print('🚀 Installing dependencies... This may take several minutes.')\\n",
    "# Install PyTorch, xformers, and flash-attn\\n",
    "!pip install torch==2.4.1 torchvision==0.19.1 torchaudio==2.4.1 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\\n",
    "!pip install -U xformers==0.0.28 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\\n",
    "!pip install misaki[en] ninja psutil packaging\\n",
    "!pip install flash_attn==2.7.4.post1\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Install other dependencies from requirements.txt and librosa\\n",
    "!pip install -r requirements.txt\\n",
    "!pip install librosa\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Install ffmpeg\\n",
    "!apt-get -qq update && apt-get install -y ffmpeg\\n",
    "print('✅ All dependencies installed.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "download_markdown_cell"
   },
   "source": [
    "### **Step 2: Download Models**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Now, let's download the pre-trained models. This is a large download (around 30 GB), so it will take a significant amount of time depending on Colab's network speed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "download_code_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('🚀 Downloading models from Hugging Face...')\\n",
    "# Note: You might need to log in to Hugging Face CLI if you haven't before.\\n",
    "# from huggingface_hub import login; login()\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Download base model\\n",
    "!huggingface-cli download Wan-AI/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P --local-dir ./weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P --local-dir-use-symlinks False\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Download audio encoder\\n",
    "!huggingface-cli download TencentGameMate/chinese-wav2vec2-base --local-dir ./weights/chinese-wav2vec2-base --local-dir-use-symlinks False\\n",
    "!huggingface-cli download TencentGameMate/chinese-wav2vec2-base model.safetensors --revision refs/pr/1 --local-dir ./weights/chinese-wav2vec2-base --local-dir-use-symlinks False\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Download TTS weights\\n",
    "!huggingface-cli download hexgrad/Kokoro-82M --local-dir ./weights/Kokoro-82M --local-dir-use-symlinks False\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Download MultiTalk weights\\n",
    "!huggingface-cli download MeiGen-AI/MeiGen-MultiTalk --local-dir ./weights/MeiGen-MultiTalk --local-dir-use-symlinks False\\n",
    "print('✅ Models downloaded.')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print('🚀 Preparing model files...')\\n",
    "# Prepare model files by copying the MultiTalk weights into the base model directory\\n",
    "!mv weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors.index.json weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors.index.json_old\\n",
    "!cp weights/MeiGen-MultiTalk/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors.index.json weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P/\\n",
    "!cp weights/MeiGen-MultiTalk/multitalk.safetensors weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P/\\n",
    "print('✅ Model files prepared.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "config_markdown_cell"
   },
   "source": [
    "### **Step 3: Configure Your Video**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Use the form below to configure the video generation. \\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Instructions:**\\n",
    "1. **Upload your files**: Use the file explorer on the left (folder icon) to upload your input image and audio files. You can create a new folder or upload to the root of the `/content/MultiTalk/` directory.\\n",
    "2. **Copy paths**: Right-click on an uploaded file and select 'Copy path'.\\n",
    "3. **Fill the form**: Paste the paths into the appropriate fields below and set the other options."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "config_code_cell",
    "colab_type": "code",
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 526
    },
    "cellView": "form"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#@title 🎬 Configure Video Generation\\n",
    "#@markdown --- \\n",
    "#@markdown ### 1. General Settings\\n",
    "generation_mode = 'Single Person' #@param [\\"Single Person\\", \\"Multi Person\\"]\\n",
    "prompt = 'A woman is passionately singing into a professional microphone in a recording studio.' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "image_path = 'examples/single/single1.png' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "\\n",
    "#@markdown ---\\n",
    "#@markdown ### 2. Audio Settings\\n",
    "audio_source = 'File Upload' #@param [\\"File Upload\\", \\"Text-to-Speech (TTS)\\" ]\\n",
    "\\n",
    "#@markdown #### **Audio from File Upload**\\n",
    "#@markdown *Used if 'Audio Source' is 'File Upload'. For Single Person mode, only Audio Path 1 is used.*\\n",
    "audio_path_1 = 'examples/single/1.wav' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "audio_path_2 = 'examples/multi/2/1.wav' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "\\n",
    "#@markdown #### **Audio from Text-to-Speech (TTS)**\\n",
    "#@markdown *Used if 'Audio Source' is 'Text-to-Speech (TTS)'.*\\n",
    "#@markdown *For Multi-Person, use `(s1)` and `(s2)` to denote speakers. e.g., `(s1) Hello! (s2) Hi there!`*\\n",
    "tts_text = '(s1) Hello, this is a test of the text to speech system.' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "#@markdown *For TTS, you must provide paths to voice reference files (.pt). Default voices are provided.*\\n",
    "tts_voice_1 = 'weights/MeiGen-MultiTalk/voices/speaker1.pt' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "tts_voice_2 = 'weights/MeiGen-MultiTalk/voices/speaker2.pt' #@param {type:\\"string\\"}\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"✅ Configuration loaded.\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Generation Mode: {generation_mode}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Prompt: {prompt}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Image Path: {image_path}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Audio Source: {audio_source}\\")\\n",
    "if audio_source == 'File Upload':\\n",
    "    print(f\\"Audio Path 1: {audio_path_1}\\")\\n",
    "    if generation_mode == 'Multi Person':\\n",
    "        print(f\\"Audio Path 2: {audio_path_2}\\")\\n",
    "else:\\n",
    "    print(f\\"TTS Text: {tts_text}\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "run_markdown_cell"
   },
   "source": [
    "### **Step 4: Generate the Video**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "This cell will now run the video generation process based on your configuration. \\n",
    "\\n",
    "It is optimized for performance on a standard Colab GPU and may take several minutes to complete."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "run_code_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\\n",
    "import os\\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Create a directory for the outputs if it doesn't exist\\n",
    "os.makedirs('outputs', exist_ok=True)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# 1. Create the input JSON data structure from the form variables\\n",
    "input_data = {\\n",
    "    'prompt': prompt,\\n",
    "    'cond_image': image_path,\\n",
    "    'cond_audio': {},\\n",
    "    'tts_audio': {},\\n",
    "    'audio_type': 'para'\\n",
    "}\\n",
    "\\n",
    "if audio_source == 'File Upload':\\n",
    "    input_data['cond_audio']['person1'] = audio_path_1\\n",
    "    if generation_mode == 'Multi Person':\\n",
    "        input_data['cond_audio']['person2'] = audio_path_2\\n",
    "else:  # Text-to-Speech\\n",
    "    input_data['tts_audio']['text'] = tts_text\\n",
    "    input_data['tts_audio']['human1_voice'] = tts_voice_1\\n",
    "    input_data['cond_audio']['person1'] = 'None'\\n",
    "    if generation_mode == 'Multi Person':\\n",
    "        input_data['tts_audio']['human2_voice'] = tts_voice_2\\n",
    "        input_data['cond_audio']['person2'] = 'None'\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# 2. Write the JSON data to a file\\n",
    "input_json_path = 'colab_input.json'\\n",
    "with open(input_json_path, 'w') as f:\\n",
    "    json.dump(input_data, f, indent=4)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f'✅ Input JSON created at {input_json_path}')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# 3. Construct the generation command\\n",
    "timestamp = datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M%S')\\n",
    "output_filename = f'outputs/colab_generation_{timestamp}'\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Download the FusioniX LoRA for acceleration if it doesn't exist\\n",
    "lora_path = 'weights/Wan2.1_I2V_14B_FusionX_LoRA.safetensors'\\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(lora_path):\\n",
    "    print('🚀 Downloading FusioniX LoRA for acceleration...')\\n",
    "    lora_url = 'https://huggingface.co/vrgamedevgirl84/Wan14BT2VFusioniX/resolve/main/FusionX_LoRa/Wan2.1_I2V_14B_FusionX_LoRA.safetensors'\\n",
    "    os.makedirs('weights', exist_ok=True)\\n",
    "    # Using wget as it's simpler than huggingface-cli for a single file\\n",
    "    !wget -q --show-progress -O {lora_path} {lora_url}\\n",
    "    print('✅ LoRA downloaded.')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "command = (\\n",
    "    'python generate_multitalk.py '\\n",
    "    f'--ckpt_dir weights/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P '\\n",
    "    f'--wav2vec_dir \\'weights/chinese-wav2vec2-base\\' '\\n",
    "    f'--input_json {input_json_path} '\\n",
    "    f'--save_file {output_filename} '\\n",
    "    # Performance optimizations for Colab\\n",
    "    f'--lora_dir {lora_path} '\\n",
    "    '--lora_scale 1.0 '\\n",
    "    '--sample_text_guide_scale 1.0 '\\n",
    "    '--sample_audio_guide_scale 2.0 '\\n",
    "    '--sample_steps 8 '\\n",
    "    '--num_persistent_param_in_dit 0 '\\n",
    "    '--sample_shift 2 '\\n",
    "    '--mode streaming '\\n",
    ")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "if audio_source == 'Text-to-Speech (TTS)':\\n",
    "    command += '--audio_mode tts'\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# 4. Execute the command\\n",
    "print('🚀 Starting video generation... This will take a few minutes.')\\n",
    "get_ipython().system(command)\\n",
    "print(f'✅ Video generation complete! Saved to {output_filename}.mp4')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Store the output file path for the next cell\\n",
    "output_video_path = f'{output_filename}.mp4'\\n",
    "with open('output_video_path.txt', 'w') as f:\\n",
    "    f.write(output_video_path)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "display_markdown_cell"
   },
   "source": [
    "### **Step 5: View Your Masterpiece!**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "The generated video will be displayed below. You can also find the video file in the `outputs` folder in the file explorer to the left."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "display_code_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\\n",
    "from IPython.display import Video, display\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Read the path of the generated video from the file created in the previous step\\n",
    "try:\\n",
    "    with open('output_video_path.txt', 'r') as f:\\n",
    "        video_path = f.read().strip()\\n",
    "    \\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(video_path):\\n",
    "        print(f'✅ Displaying video from: {video_path}')\\n",
    "        # Display the video, embedded in the notebook\\n",
    "        display(Video(video_path, embed=True, width=512))\\n",
    "    else:\\n",
    "        print(f'❌ Error: Video file not found at {video_path}')\\n",
    "        print('Please check the output of the previous cell for any errors during generation.')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\\n",
    "    print('❌ Error: Could not find the output path file. Did the previous cell run correctly?')\\n"
   ]
  }
